  "limitations": [
    "The background and halo tracer are initially cored; this experiment cannot demonstrate cusp removal.",
    "Halo and stellar populations are tracers in a prescribed field; neither an updating gravitational field nor a self-consistent final density is calculated.",
    "The stationary central energy tag excludes weakly bound orbits that pass through the center and is not the instantaneous mass inside radius2 or a core-energy requirement.",
    "The star population is mildly warm and stationary, but its matched guiding-radius law has a central surface-density hole and is not a typical exponential disk.",
    "The ratio is per unit stellar and tagged halo mass. A total energy cost requires the stellar/halo mass ratio and the tag mass fraction; it is not an observational overheating bound.",
    "The spherical force preserves angular momenta and protects vertical actions; this does not test disk vertical survival under realistic feedback.",
    "Empirical sample intervals and selected numerical references do not certify unseen continuum tails.",
    "The weak pulse deposits only about3 parts per million of the tag mean binding energy. Energetically effective repeated or nonlinear histories are untested.",
    "Gas motion remains a kinematic positive-density construction, without pressure dynamics, a feedback energy source or a hydrodynamic implementation.",
    "The gas second-derivative edge and finite time window contribute spectral tails; no infinite-frequency scaling is inferred.",
    "A cuspy Hernquist halo has no finite circular-frequency maximum and must be tested separately with a centrally populated stellar disk."
  ],
